# 14 October 2026: the rhythm method sheet on the ADJUDICATED references (and the synthetic videos for the transitions).
# Twenty methods, four phases each, one truth, leave-one-reference-out: a method is tuned on the other references and judged on the
# held-out one, so a number is always a number on a video the method never saw.
#   P1 signal      the number per boundary, scored by the area under the ROC curve of true cuts against (a) every boundary,
#                  (b) the judged traps (boundaries an eye called "not a cut");
#   P2 candidates  peak picking (adaptive or global), scored F1 at +-1 frame;
#   P3 verify      persistence, flash return, isolation, F1 at +-1 frame;
#   P4 place       exact frame, F1 at 0 and at +-1 frame.
# M01-M15 single signals, M16-M18 transitions, M19 the area-rule conjunction, M20 the learned fusion (rhythm_fusion).
# Run:  nice -n 5 /Users/zenray/.venvs/zenray-motion/bin/python -I Scripts/RhythmSheet.py run [--json out.json] [--md out.md]
#       ... train        (fit the fusion on every adjudicated reference and write datasets/rhythm-fusion.json)
# FR : la feuille de methodes sur les references adjudiquees : vingt methodes, quatre phases, validation par reference exclue.
